SELECT v.id, c.id, $t$Best Tonneau Covers for 2019–2025 Ram 1500 DT (5'7" / 6'4" Bed, RamBox Guide)$t$, $m$Ram 1500 DT tonneau covers by bed length, with a clear split between standard beds and RamBox-equipped trucks.$m$, $i$The DT Ram has two beds — 5'7" (67 in) and 6'4" (76 in) — and the single biggest fit question is RamBox. RamBox trucks have a narrower bed opening with factory rails, so they need RamBox-specific covers. Everything below is labelled standard or RamBox.$i$, $g$- **RamBox** = separate SKU. A standard-bed cover will not seal on a RamBox truck and vice-versa.
- **Ram 1500 Classic (DS)** was sold alongside the DT through 2024 — it has the older bed and different covers. Check the tailgate badge: DT has the 'RAM' letters across the gate.
- **Multifunction (split) tailgate** works with roll-ups and most tri-folds; a few hard covers need a spacer kit.
- **TRX / RHO** use the 5'7" bed and standard covers.$g$, $f$[{"q": "How do I know if my Ram has RamBox?", "a": "Lockable storage bins built into the bed sides above the wheel wells. If you have them, buy RamBox-specific covers only."}, {"q": "Does a 5'7\" DT cover fit the Ram 1500 Classic?", "a": "No. The Classic uses the 2009–2018 bed; buy DS-specific covers."}, {"q": "Is the multifunction tailgate a problem?", "a": "Only for a few hard covers that rely on a full-width tailgate seal. Roll-ups and tri-folds are fine."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Standard bed:** hard tri-fold. **RamBox:** RamBox-specific roll-up or tri-fold — fewer choices, so buy on reviews. **Premium:** retractable, standard beds only.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
FROM vehicles v JOIN makes m ON m.id=v.make_id JOIN categories c ON c.slug='tonneau-covers'
