SELECT v.id, c.id, $t$Best Tonneau Covers for 2022–2025 Toyota Tundra (5.5 / 6.5 / 8.1 ft Bed)$t$, $m$Fit-verified tonneau covers for the 3rd-gen Tundra's composite bed, by bed length, with deck-rail notes.$m$, $i$The 2022+ Tundra has a composite bed with a factory deck-rail system on three lengths: 5.5 ft (66 in), 6.5 ft (79 in) and 8.1 ft (98 in). The deck rails sit inside the bed rail cap, so most clamp-on covers fit, but the composite rail cap dents easier than steel — use rubber-padded clamps.$i$, $g$- **2007–2021 Tundra covers do not fit** — the bed and rails changed completely in 2022.
- **Deck rail cleats** must be slid out of the way or removed for clamp-style rails on some covers.
- **TRD Pro / Capstone** share beds with the rest of the range.
- **Composite rail cap**: over-tightened metal clamps crack it. Torque to the cover maker's spec.$g$, $f$[{"q": "Which Tundra bed do I have?", "a": "CrewMax = 5.5 ft standard, 6.5 ft optional; Double Cab = 6.5 ft or 8.1 ft. Measure inside the bed."}, {"q": "Do I need to remove the deck rails?", "a": "No — the rails are inside the bed. Only the sliding cleats may need repositioning."}, {"q": "Hard or soft for a hybrid Tundra?", "a": "No difference — the i-FORCE MAX has no bed-mounted hardware."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** soft roll-up with padded clamps. **Best overall:** hard tri-fold listed for 2022+. **Premium:** retractable.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
