SELECT v.id, c.id, $t$Best Roof Racks & Crossbars for 2010–2024 Toyota 4Runner (Raised Rails vs TRD Pro)$t$, $m$Crossbars, platforms and baskets verified for the 5th-gen 4Runner's raised rails, with a separate answer for TRD Pro.$m$, $i$Most 5th-gen 4Runners have factory raised rails — crossbar kits clamp on with no drilling. TRD Pro trims ship with a factory basket rack instead, which needs basket-specific mounts. Roof load is 165 lb dynamic; that caps rooftop tents to lightweight softshells.$i$, $g$- **TRD Pro** = factory basket, no raised rails. Buy TRD-Pro-listed mounts.
- **165 lb dynamic roof load**: a 130 lb hardshell tent plus crossbars is at the limit — use the bed of a truck or a lightweight tent.
- **Sunroof**: rear crossbar must clear the glass when opened; most kits place it behind.
- **Rear window roll-down** is unaffected by racks.$g$, $f$[{"q": "Do I need to drill for a 4Runner rack?", "a": "No — raised-rail clamp crossbars or a full platform on the rails."}, {"q": "Can I put a rooftop tent on a 4Runner?", "a": "Lightweight ones (under ~120 lb) on a full-length platform; heavy hardshells exceed the 165 lb rating."}, {"q": "Do 5th-gen racks fit the 2025 4Runner?", "a": "No — new roof geometry. See the 2025+ page."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** aero crossbars on raised rails. **Best overall:** low-profile full-length platform. **TRD Pro:** basket-compatible platform adapter.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
FROM vehicles v JOIN makes m ON m.id=v.make_id JOIN categories c ON c.slug='roof-racks'
