SELECT v.id, c.id, $t$Best Roof Racks for 2020–2025 Tesla Model Y (Fixed-Point Glass Roof, Juniper Included)$t$, $m$Roof racks that mount to the Model Y's four fixed points — the only safe way to carry loads on the glass roof.$m$, $i$The Model Y has a panoramic glass roof with four hidden fixed mounting points under plastic caps. Only fixed-point crossbar kits fit — no clamp bars, no door-jamb bars, ever. Tesla's own rack and a handful of aftermarket kits use these points. The 2025 Juniper refresh keeps the same mount points.$i$, $g$- **Never use door-jamb or clamp crossbars** on the glass roof.
- **Juniper (2025+)** uses the same fixed points; listings that say 2020–2024 usually fit but confirm.
- **Load limit 165 lb** dynamic; tents are not recommended by Tesla.
- **Range**: expect a 5–10% hit with bars, more with a box.$g$, $f$[{"q": "Do Model 3 racks fit the Model Y?", "a": "No — different fixed-point spacing."}, {"q": "Can I leave the rack on?", "a": "Yes, but it costs range; remove when not needed."}, {"q": "Will a rack void the warranty?", "a": "Fixed-point kits used within the load rating do not; glass damage from clamp bars does."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** aftermarket fixed-point crossbars. **Best overall:** Tesla-spec bars with a low-drag box. **Bike carrier:** hitch mount instead of roof.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
