- **Hatch clearance** is generous on the Outback; most boxes under 90 in are fine.
- **Wilderness**: use ladder-rack mounts, not clamp bars.
- **176 lb roof load** limit.$g$, $f$[{"q": "Can I mount a cargo box on the factory Outback crossbars?", "a": "Yes if the box's mounting slots match the factory bar spread; most 12–16 cu ft boxes do."}, {"q": "Do I need aftermarket bars?", "a": "For 18+ cu ft boxes or frequent use, yes — stiffer and adjustable spread."}, {"q": "Will the box work with a sunroof?", "a": "Yes; place the front bar so the sunroof tilts without touching."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** 13 cu ft box on factory bars. **Best overall:** 16 cu ft on aftermarket bars. **Wilderness:** rack-mounted box up to 18 cu ft.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
