SELECT v.id, c.id, $t$Best Tonneau Covers for 2024–2025 Toyota Tacoma (4th Gen, 5 ft & 6 ft Bed)$t$, $m$Tonneau covers with confirmed 2024+ Tacoma fitment — the new composite bed and deck rails do not accept 2016–2023 covers.$m$, $i$The 4th-gen Tacoma keeps a composite bed with deck rails, but the bed rail cap and width changed, so 2016–2023 covers do not fit. Two beds: 5 ft (60 in) and 6 ft (74 in). Hybrid i-FORCE MAX trucks share the bed.$i$, $g$- **2016–2023 covers do not fit.**
- **Deck rail cleats** may need sliding for clamp-style side rails.
- **Composite rail cap**: padded clamps, torque to spec.
- **Trailhunter / TRD Pro** share the bed; Trailhunter's bed utility bar conflicts with some hard covers.$g$, $f$[{"q": "Can I reuse a 3rd-gen Tacoma cover?", "a": "No — bed width and rail cap changed in 2024."}, {"q": "Which Tacoma trims have the 6 ft bed?", "a": "Xtracab (2-door) and some SR/SR5 Double Cab builds; measure to confirm."}, {"q": "Does the hybrid change anything?", "a": "No bed-mounted hardware; same covers."}]$f$::jsonb, $v$**Budget:** soft roll-up listed for 2024+. **Best overall:** hard tri-fold with confirmed 2024+ fit. **Premium:** retractable as fitments arrive.$v$, 'draft', CURRENT_DATE
FROM vehicles v JOIN makes m ON m.id=v.make_id JOIN categories c ON c.slug='tonneau-covers'
